# The root R0 without an entry: the root code executes by itself, the Structures are root-code records (`@: Name (...)`),
# and the written call stands after the reached declarations. `b := 1` in `Add\add` changes the root place b of the
# same root activation; `Log\seen` 1; the file DATA keeps its written value, `b` 0. The same on the sets S1 and S2.
# Norm: the book #root-activation; #structural-call (the scope of the caller is not limited by the new frame).
@: Log (
    int: seen 0
)
int: b 0
@: Add (
    add:
        b := 1
    end: add
)
Add\add()
Log\seen := b
